@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il33-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il33-readings`
IMPORT `nii-ss69-69a-71`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests: ss 69, 69A, 71. Row IL-33. Every expected value was worked by hand from the Hebrew
-- (lines 836-851) before the run; the working is beside each group.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN parents IS A `The parents of a child, for section 69`
      alone   IS A BOOLEAN
      entitled IS A BOOLEAN
      asked   IS A BOOLEAN
      guardian IS A BOOLEAN
      appointee IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The facts of section 69`
`facts of section 69: parents` parents `, with the father only` alone `, father entitled` entitled `, asked` asked `, guardian` guardian `, appointee` appointee MEANS
    `The facts of section 69` WITH
        `the parents`                                                                                IS parents
        `the child is with the father only`                                                          IS alone
        `the father is entitled to the allowance`                                                    IS entitled
        `the parent paid under section 69(a) asked that the allowance be paid to the other parent`   IS asked
        `a guardian was lawfully appointed`                                                          IS guardian
        `a person was appointed under section 304(a)`                                                IS appointee
        `the Institute's decision under section 69(d)`                                               IS NOTHING

GIVEN f IS A `The facts of section 69`
      d IS A `A decision of the Institute under section 69(d)`
GIVETH A `The facts of section 69`
f `with the decision` d MEANS
    `The facts of section 69` WITH
        `the parents`                                                                                IS f's `the parents`
        `the child is with the father only`                                                          IS f's `the child is with the father only`
        `the father is entitled to the allowance`                                                    IS f's `the father is entitled to the allowance`
        `the parent paid under section 69(a) asked that the allowance be paid to the other parent`   IS f's `the parent paid under section 69(a) asked that the allowance be paid to the other parent`
        `a guardian was lawfully appointed`                                                          IS f's `a guardian was lawfully appointed`
        `a person was appointed under section 304(a)`                                                IS f's `a person was appointed under section 304(a)`
        `the Institute's decision under section 69(d)`                                               IS JUST d

GIVEN n IS A STRING
      d IS A DATE
      m IS A STRING
      p IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A child of a man with children by several women`
`a child` n `born` d `of` m `, mother proved:` p MEANS
    `A child of a man with children by several women` WITH
        `name`                                                                                                    IS n
        `date of birth`                                                                                           IS d
        `the name of the child's mother`                                                                          IS m
        `the mother proved to the Institute's satisfaction that she keeps no joint household with the father and that the child does not depend on his table` IS p

GIVEN fatherFirst IS A BOOLEAN
      second      IS A MAYBE STRING
      entitled    IS A BOOLEAN
      secondGone  IS A BOOLEAN
      secondDay   IS A MAYBE DATE
      withMother  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `The facts of section 71`
`facts of section 71: first is the father` fatherFirst `, second parent` second `, entitled` entitled `, also gone` secondGone `, on` secondDay `, with the mother only` withMother MEANS
    `The facts of section 71` WITH
        `the name of the parent who died or ceased to be insured`  IS "First"
        `that parent is the child's father`                        IS fatherFirst
        `the day he or she died or ceased to be insured`           IS YMD 2020 1 1
        `the name of the child's second parent`                    IS second
        `the second parent is entitled to the child allowance`     IS entitled
        `the second parent also died or ceased to be insured`      IS secondGone
        `the day the second parent died or ceased to be insured`   IS secondDay
        `the child is with the mother only`                        IS withMother

§ `Tests — s 69 (to whom the allowance is paid)`

-- (a) the mother; the father only if the child is with him only and he is entitled.
#ASSERT `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` (`facts of section 69: parents` `a mother and a father` `, with the father only` FALSE `, father entitled` TRUE `, asked` FALSE `, guardian` FALSE `, appointee` FALSE) EQUALS `the mother`
#ASSERT `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` (`facts of section 69: parents` `a mother and a father` `, with the father only` TRUE `, father entitled` TRUE `, asked` FALSE `, guardian` FALSE `, appointee` FALSE) EQUALS `the father`
#ASSERT `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` (`facts of section 69: parents` `a mother and a father` `, with the father only` TRUE `, father entitled` FALSE `, asked` FALSE `, guardian` FALSE `, appointee` FALSE) EQUALS `the mother`
#ASSERT `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` (`facts of section 69: parents` `a mother only` `, with the father only` FALSE `, father entitled` FALSE `, asked` FALSE `, guardian` FALSE `, appointee` FALSE) EQUALS `the mother`
-- A father alone: paid if the child is with him and he is entitled; otherwise (c).
#ASSERT `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` (`facts of section 69: parents` `a father only` `, with the father only` TRUE `, father entitled` TRUE `, asked` FALSE `, guardian` FALSE `, appointee` FALSE) EQUALS `the father`
#ASSERT `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` (`facts of section 69: parents` `a father only` `, with the father only` TRUE `, father entitled` FALSE `, asked` FALSE `, guardian` TRUE `, appointee` TRUE) EQUALS `the guardian lawfully appointed`
#ASSERT `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` (`facts of section 69: parents` `a father only` `, with the father only` TRUE `, father entitled` FALSE `, asked` FALSE `, guardian` FALSE `, appointee` TRUE) EQUALS `the person appointed under section 304(a)`
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` (`facts of section 69: parents` `a father only` `, with the father only` TRUE `, father entitled` FALSE `, asked` FALSE `, guardian` FALSE `, appointee` FALSE)
-- (c) a child with no parent: the guardian, and without one the appointee.
#ASSERT `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` (`facts of section 69: parents` `no parent` `, with the father only` FALSE `, father entitled` FALSE `, asked` FALSE `, guardian` TRUE `, appointee` TRUE) EQUALS `the guardian lawfully appointed`
#ASSERT `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` (`facts of section 69: parents` `no parent` `, with the father only` FALSE `, father entitled` FALSE `, asked` FALSE `, guardian` FALSE `, appointee` TRUE) EQUALS `the person appointed under section 304(a)`
-- Two parents of one sex: declined by name (fork P1).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` (`facts of section 69: parents` `two parents of one sex` `, with the father only` FALSE `, father entitled` FALSE `, asked` FALSE `, guardian` FALSE `, appointee` FALSE)
-- (b) the parent paid under (a) asks that the other parent be paid.
#ASSERT `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` (`facts of section 69: parents` `a mother and a father` `, with the father only` FALSE `, father entitled` TRUE `, asked` TRUE `, guardian` FALSE `, appointee` FALSE) EQUALS `the other parent, at the request of the parent paid under section 69(a)`
-- A request where (a) paid a guardian: there is no parent paid under (a).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` (`facts of section 69: parents` `no parent` `, with the father only` FALSE `, father entitled` FALSE `, asked` TRUE `, guardian` TRUE `, appointee` FALSE)
-- (d) the Institute's decision, in the welfare of the child.
#ASSERT `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` ((`facts of section 69: parents` `a mother and a father` `, with the father only` FALSE `, father entitled` TRUE `, asked` FALSE `, guardian` FALSE `, appointee` FALSE) `with the decision` `to pay the guardian`) EQUALS `the guardian lawfully appointed`
#ASSERT `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` ((`facts of section 69: parents` `a mother and a father` `, with the father only` FALSE `, father entitled` TRUE `, asked` FALSE `, guardian` FALSE `, appointee` FALSE) `with the decision` `to pay a second parent who is not entitled`) EQUALS `a second parent who is not entitled, by decision of the Institute`
#ASSERT `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` ((`facts of section 69: parents` `a mother and a father` `, with the father only` FALSE `, father entitled` TRUE `, asked` FALSE `, guardian` FALSE `, appointee` FALSE) `with the decision` `to pay the person appointed under section 304(a)`) EQUALS `the person appointed under section 304(a)`
-- (b) and (d) together (fork P2): declined by default; each reading by name.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` ((`facts of section 69: parents` `a mother and a father` `, with the father only` FALSE `, father entitled` TRUE `, asked` TRUE `, guardian` FALSE `, appointee` FALSE) `with the decision` `to pay the guardian`)
#ASSERT `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` ((`facts of section 69: parents` `a mother and a father` `, with the father only` FALSE `, father entitled` TRUE `, asked` TRUE `, guardian` FALSE `, appointee` FALSE) `with the decision` `to pay the guardian`) `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `a request under section 69(b) and a decision under section 69(d)` `read as` `the request under section 69(b) prevails`) EQUALS `the other parent, at the request of the parent paid under section 69(a)`
#ASSERT `s 69 — the person to whom the child allowance is paid, in` ((`facts of section 69: parents` `a mother and a father` `, with the father only` FALSE `, father entitled` TRUE `, asked` TRUE `, guardian` FALSE `, appointee` FALSE) `with the decision` `to pay the guardian`) `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `a request under section 69(b) and a decision under section 69(d)` `read as` `the decision under section 69(d) prevails`) EQUALS `the guardian lawfully appointed`

§ `Tests — s 69A (children by several women)`

-- Case A: five children, M1 the mother of three (1 January 1999, 1 January 2001, 1 January 2002), M2 of two
-- (1 June 2000, 1 December 2002). All five were born before 1 June 2003. In the count of all the man's
-- children, five (four or more) were born before that day: s 69A(1) applies. In each woman's count, M1 has
-- three and M2 two: neither reaches four, so (1) does not apply and (2) does. The readings differ.
caseA MEANS LIST `a child` "a1" `born` (YMD 1999 1 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE,
                 `a child` "a2" `born` (YMD 2001 1 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE,
                 `a child` "a3" `born` (YMD 2002 1 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE,
                 `a child` "b1" `born` (YMD 2000 6 1) `of` "M2" `, mother proved:` FALSE,
                 `a child` "b2" `born` (YMD 2002 12 1) `of` "M2" `, mother proved:` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 69A — the man has children by more than one woman:` caseA
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 69A(1) — the man has a child as in section 68(b):` caseA `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT `s 69A(1) — the man has a child as in section 68(b):` caseA `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `a child as in section 68(b), for section 69A(1)` `read as` `measured in the count of all the man's children`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 69A(1) — the man has a child as in section 68(b):` caseA `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `a child as in section 68(b), for section 69A(1)` `read as` `measured in the count of each woman's children`)
-- On the first reading every child is in its own mother's count (1).
#ASSERT `s 69A — the count in which` (`a child` "a1" `born` (YMD 1999 1 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE) `comes, among` caseA `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `a child as in section 68(b), for section 69A(1)` `read as` `measured in the count of all the man's children`) EQUALS `the count of its mother`
-- On the second, (2): in the father's count, unless the mother proved what (2) asks: b2's mother did.
#ASSERT `s 69A — the count in which` (`a child` "a1" `born` (YMD 1999 1 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE) `comes, among` caseA `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `a child as in section 68(b), for section 69A(1)` `read as` `measured in the count of each woman's children`) EQUALS `the count of the father`
#ASSERT `s 69A — the count in which` (`a child` "b2" `born` (YMD 2002 12 1) `of` "M2" `, mother proved:` TRUE) `comes, among` caseA `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `a child as in section 68(b), for section 69A(1)` `read as` `measured in the count of each woman's children`) EQUALS `the count of its mother`
-- By default the question for a1 is declined (the readings put it in different counts).
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 69A — the count in which` (`a child` "a1" `born` (YMD 1999 1 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE) `comes, among` caseA

-- Case B: four children of M1 alone-plus-one of M2: M1 has four born before 1 June 2003: both readings agree
-- that (1) applies (the man has four, and M1 has four). The default answers.
caseB MEANS LIST `a child` "a1" `born` (YMD 1996 1 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE,
                 `a child` "a2" `born` (YMD 1998 1 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE,
                 `a child` "a3" `born` (YMD 2000 1 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE,
                 `a child` "a4" `born` (YMD 2003 5 31) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE,
                 `a child` "b1" `born` (YMD 2010 1 1) `of` "M2" `, mother proved:` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 69A(1) — the man has a child as in section 68(b):` caseB `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT `s 69A — the count in which` (`a child` "b1" `born` (YMD 2010 1 1) `of` "M2" `, mother proved:` FALSE) `comes, among` caseB EQUALS `the count of its mother`
-- The edge of the date: the fourth born on 1 June 2003 instead of 31 May 2003 is not "before 1 June 2003":
-- M1 then has three, the man three, and nobody has a child as in s 68(b): the children are the father's.
caseB2 MEANS LIST `a child` "a1" `born` (YMD 1996 1 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE,
                  `a child` "a2" `born` (YMD 1998 1 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE,
                  `a child` "a3" `born` (YMD 2000 1 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE,
                  `a child` "a4" `born` (YMD 2003 6 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE,
                  `a child` "b1" `born` (YMD 2010 1 1) `of` "M2" `, mother proved:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 69A(1) — the man has a child as in section 68(b):` caseB2 `, reading` `the readings this row takes`
#ASSERT `s 69A — the count in which` (`a child` "b1" `born` (YMD 2010 1 1) `of` "M2" `, mother proved:` FALSE) `comes, among` caseB2 EQUALS `the count of the father`

-- Case C: young children by two women: (2); the mother who proves is in her own count.
caseC MEANS LIST `a child` "a1" `born` (YMD 2015 1 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE,
                 `a child` "b1" `born` (YMD 2017 1 1) `of` "M2" `, mother proved:` TRUE
#ASSERT `s 69A — the count in which` (`a child` "a1" `born` (YMD 2015 1 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE) `comes, among` caseC EQUALS `the count of the father`
#ASSERT `s 69A — the count in which` (`a child` "b1" `born` (YMD 2017 1 1) `of` "M2" `, mother proved:` TRUE) `comes, among` caseC EQUALS `the count of its mother`
-- One woman only: s 69A does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT `s 69A — the man has children by more than one woman:` (LIST `a child` "a1" `born` (YMD 2015 1 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE, `a child` "a2" `born` (YMD 2017 1 1) `of` "M1" `, mother proved:` FALSE)

§ `Tests — s 71 (a parent who died or ceased to be insured)`

-- One parent only: by virtue of the parent who died or ceased to be insured.
#ASSERT `s 71 — by virtue of whom, in` (`facts of section 71: first is the father` TRUE `, second parent` NOTHING `, entitled` FALSE `, also gone` FALSE `, on` NOTHING `, with the mother only` FALSE) EQUALS `by virtue of the parent who died or ceased to be insured`
-- A second parent who is entitled: by virtue of the second parent (the proviso).
#ASSERT `s 71 — by virtue of whom, in` (`facts of section 71: first is the father` TRUE `, second parent` (JUST "Second") `, entitled` TRUE `, also gone` FALSE `, on` NOTHING `, with the mother only` FALSE) EQUALS `by virtue of the second parent`
-- A second parent who is not entitled (excluded by s 66, say): the proviso does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 71 — by virtue of whom, in` (`facts of section 71: first is the father` TRUE `, second parent` (JUST "Second") `, entitled` FALSE `, also gone` FALSE `, on` NOTHING `, with the mother only` FALSE) EQUALS `by virtue of the parent who died or ceased to be insured`
-- Both gone (fork S1). First died 1 January 2020, second 1 January 2021. First named is the father; the child
-- is with both: s 67(b) would choose the father = the first; the first to go is the first: both readings
-- agree, so the default answers.
#ASSERT `s 71 — by virtue of whom, in` (`facts of section 71: first is the father` TRUE `, second parent` (JUST "Second") `, entitled` FALSE `, also gone` TRUE `, on` (JUST (YMD 2021 1 1)) `, with the mother only` FALSE) EQUALS `by virtue of the parent who died or ceased to be insured`
-- The child is with the mother only: s 67(b) would choose the mother = the second; the first to go is the
-- first: the readings differ.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 71 — by virtue of whom, in` (`facts of section 71: first is the father` TRUE `, second parent` (JUST "Second") `, entitled` FALSE `, also gone` TRUE `, on` (JUST (YMD 2021 1 1)) `, with the mother only` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 71 — by virtue of whom, in` (`facts of section 71: first is the father` TRUE `, second parent` (JUST "Second") `, entitled` FALSE `, also gone` TRUE `, on` (JUST (YMD 2021 1 1)) `, with the mother only` TRUE) `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `section 71 where both parents died or ceased to be insured` `read as` `by virtue of the parent s 67(b) would choose if both were alive and insured`) EQUALS `by virtue of the second parent`
#ASSERT `s 71 — by virtue of whom, in` (`facts of section 71: first is the father` TRUE `, second parent` (JUST "Second") `, entitled` FALSE `, also gone` TRUE `, on` (JUST (YMD 2021 1 1)) `, with the mother only` TRUE) `, reading` (`the readings` `the readings this row takes` `with` `section 71 where both parents died or ceased to be insured` `read as` `by virtue of the parent who died or ceased to be insured first`) EQUALS `by virtue of the parent who died or ceased to be insured`
-- Both gone on one day: the "first" reading cannot say; the default is declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 71 — by virtue of whom, in` (`facts of section 71: first is the father` TRUE `, second parent` (JUST "Second") `, entitled` FALSE `, also gone` TRUE `, on` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) `, with the mother only` FALSE)
-- Both gone, no day for the second: declined.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 71 — by virtue of whom, in` (`facts of section 71: first is the father` TRUE `, second parent` (JUST "Second") `, entitled` FALSE `, also gone` TRUE `, on` NOTHING `, with the mother only` FALSE)
